        <p>DIZUNICENNEN.—George Jackson and Elizabeth Stead- man were each fined as. fld. and costs for this offence. CHIMNEY ON FIELE.—ThOM2L3 iHarrison, Gladstone-st., and John H. Bushell, James-st., were each fined is. and costs for having their chimneys on fire. UNSLUZZLED DOGS.—Enoch Pitt, of Pittville Terrace. and Hugh Jones, of Moor-lane, were each fined le. and co..ts for not having their dogs securely muzzled. BREACITSS OF THH PHACE.—JHUIPS flindley, of Nelson- at., and James Boyd, of Walinsley-st., were charged with this offence. Both defendants were brfund over in £5 to keep the peace for three months, or go to goal for 7 days. CRUELTY TO A HORSF.—John Hewitt, of Warrington- road, wa4 summoned for causing a horse to I:ie worked whilst in an unfit state, and Thomas tilynne, was sum- moned for working the horse. The animal suffered from lameness and sores. Flewitt was fined 203. and costs and Wynne was ordered to pay the costa. POACHHRS.—RichArd Beswick and George Hunt, both of Ditton, were summoned for trespassing in pursuit of zarne on land belonging to Mr. Stapleton-Bretherton,at Rainhill, on the 13th inst.—Mr. J. 0. Swift, of St. Helens, appeared for the prosecution. A fine of £1 and costs, or in default a month's imprisonment, was in- flicted in each case.</p>
