      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-03-31_WidnesExaminer_art0144" n="art0144">
        <head>WESTON.</head>
        <p>WESTON.</p>
        <p>HELP POW IEI3 CPII7I2CII BEAM BAND. —With a view to augmenting the funds of the Church brass band an en- tertainment was given on Tuesday evening in the school room, Weston, tile Rev. W. Stables occupying the chair. Ther was a large attendance A programme of caPital inuEic was gone through in a most praiseworthy mariner, the accompanist being Mr.ti.llirkett Musgrove, Runcorn.</p>
        <p>MENTINO OF RATOPAVER44.—At the annual meetinz of the township, under the chairmanship of Mr. Thotnas Ford, sen. Messrs. E. Aar )n, T. Fr l, sen., J. Ford, and T. Griffiths were nominated overseers for the township. This was all the business of public interest, and the pro- ceedings closed with thank.; to the Chairman.</p>
        <p>VESTRY MEETING.—Tho annual vestry meetinx Wafi held on Wednesday evening, thn Rev. D. S minders pre- siding. The accounts showed a deficit of Ll 24. Cq 1., and the following gentlemen were chosen for the eniu- ing year :—Vicar's warden, Mr. John Jeffs ; pe.,ople's warden, Mr. L. Rowel:kers! ; sidesmen. Mr. R. C. Rezen - berg, 9. Bertliford, ana H. Ram. This concluded the business.</p>
        <p>The following advertiseinent appeared in a London morning paper :—" Wand, by a ~,entleman wit() is under covenant to leave his house precisely as he found it, 20,000 healthy fleas. Cash on delivery, middle of March. Letters only.—Ba^riatcr, care of--, road, W."</p>
