        <p>A PENNY SAVED IS A PENNY MADE. How to save money. Waste not. want not. Don't furnish on the hire system, with its extravagant high prices, arbitrary agreements, and despotic restrictions. For instance, suppose A furnishes for £lOO on the hire system with B and pays B £99 in instalments, but neglects to pay B the last instalment In time, the agreement gives B the power to forcibly retake possession of the furniture, but the whole of the £93 paid is then forfeited to B, consequently B gets both money and goods. In addition to the above disadvantages the price charged is exhorbitant, often 200 and 30 per cent more than for cash at a proper establishment. It is high time this system was dc • lar,d illegal. Be it known that at Worsley's "The Fantheon," Gaythorn, Manchester, high-class New and Second-hand Furniture may be had at the exact advertised marked cash price, no less under any circumstances. Also, that in cases where it is inconvenient to pay the whole of the money down, Worsley's are prepared to assist purchasers by allowing the aecount to be I aid .at convenient intervals, charging only a small percentage for the privilege. By this means the purchaser knows exactly what he is charged for the goods. and escapes all fear and trembling as to the loss of his furniture i he happens to miss a payment. Worsley's have on view complete Houses of Furniture for £l5, £2O, £25, £32 10s.. and £45 un.to £l,OOO, full particulars of which are supplied on application post free. "The Pantheon " is packed from floor to ceiling with countless bargains in Dining, Draw- ing. bitting, rind Bedroom Furniture, Office and Library Furniture, by Lamb, GiIIOWS, Ogden, Garnett, &amp;c. Read the following sample bargains r—High-class Second-hand Dining. room Furniture, consisting of a massive suite of nine pieces, six heavy carved single chairs, large comfortable couch, and a pair of luxurious upholstered easy chairs, by Henry Ogden and Sons ; cost £75; price for quick sale, £25. Equal to New. The Sideboard to match is by Maple, beautifully carved ; cost £120; for £2O. Dining Table and Overmantel to match, for £lO —W. H. WOR4LEY, "The Pantheon," Gaythorn, Man- chester.—See also advertisement on 4th page.</p>
